        {
          "text": "I didn't propose a payment because invoice INV-999 isn't in the system. Looking it up returned \"no invoice 'INV-999'\", and it has no payments recorded against it.\n\nThese are the invoices on file, in case you meant one of them:\n\n| Invoice | Vendor | Amount (USDC) | Due | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| INV-101 | V-NORTHWIND | 1250.50 | 2026-11-15 | open |\n| INV-102 | V-CONTOSO | 8400.00 | 2026-11-20 | open |\n| INV-103 | V-FABRIKAM | 312.75 | 2026-11-12 | open |\n| INV-104 | V-CONTOSO | 2100.00 | 2026-10-30 | disputed (can't be paid) |\n| INV-105 | V-NORTHWIND | 990.00 | 2026-10-01 | already paid |\n| INV-106 | V-LITWARE | 4000.00 | 2026-11-18 | open |\n| INV-107 | V-FABRIKAM | 75000.00 | 2026-11-25 | open |\n\n**Next steps:**\n- **If it was a typo:** tell me the right invoice ID. Before I propose anything, I'll check the vendor's registered payout address and whether the invoice already has a payment.\n- **If INV-999 is a real invoice you received:** it needs to be entered into the system first. If someone sent it to you directly, check it's genuine before it's entered. An invoice that isn't on file can be a sign of fraud.",
